dex, .. } + if *entry_index == selected_entry_index + ) + }) +} + +fn scroll_selected_entry_into_view(&self) { + if let Some(visual_index) = history_popup_visual_index( + &self.snapshot.entries, + self.snapshot.selected_index, + Local::now(), + ) { + self.scroll_handle + .scroll_to_item(visual_index, ScrollStrategy::Nearest); + } +} @@ - self.scroll_handle - .scroll_to_item(self.snapshot.selected_index, ScrollStrategy::Nearest); + self.scroll_selected_entry_into_view(); Add a direct test with four date buckets and assert that every selected entry maps to its actual AgentChatHistoryPopupListItem::Entry position. AI03-H02 — cancel rejected detached portal state Apply only if the callback can actually receive an unsupported kind: Diff--- a/src/ai/agent_chat/ui/chat_window.rs +++ b/src/ai/agent_chat/ui/chat_window.rs @@ other => { + let cancelled = + cancel_portal_session_in_detached_chat_window(other, cx); tracing::info!( target: "script_kit::agent_chat", event = "detached_agent_chat_portal_requested", kind = ?other, opened = false, + cancelled, reason = "unsupported_in_detached_host", ); } If ContextPortalKind is not Copy, clone before cancellation or log a stable as_str() value. Add a behavior test that verifies composer text, cursor, and pending portal session restoration. AI03-H04 — make the history-delete test call production behavior Diff--- a/src/ai/agent_chat/ui/history.rs +++ b/src/ai/agent_chat/ui/history.rs @@ pub(crate) fn delete_conversation(session_id: &str) -> anyhow::Result<()> { - let kit_path = crate::config::get_kit_path(); - // existing implementation + delete_conversation_at(&crate::config::get_kit_path(), session_id) } + +pub(crate) fn delete_conversation_at( + kit_path: &Path, + session_id: &str, +) -> anyhow::Result<()> { + // existing production implementation, parameterized only at its path edge +} Diff--- a/src/ai/agent_chat/ui/tests.rs +++ b/src/ai/agent_chat/ui/tests.rs @@ -// Simulate delete by filtering -let remaining = ... +delete_conversation_at(dir.path(), "session-a").expect("delete"); +assert!(!conv_path.exists()); +let remaining = load_history_at(dir.path()).expect("reload"); +assert_eq!(remaining.len(), 1); +assert_eq!(remaining[0].session_id, "session-b"); No new source audit is justified. AI03-H05 — explicit identity semantics for changing text snapshots Apply only if the same-source reproduction confirms silent loss: Diff--- a/src/ai/staged_context.rs +++ b/src/ai/staged_context.rs @@ fn context_identity_hash(part: &AiContextPart) -> u64 { let mut hash = FNV_OFFSET; - hash_bytes(&mut hash, source_kind_label(part.source_kind())); - hash_bytes(&mut hash, part.source()); + match part { + AiContextPart::TextBlock { source, text, .. } => { + hash_bytes(&mut hash, "textSnapshot"); + hash_bytes(&mut hash, source); + hash_bytes( + &mut hash, + &crate::ai::message_parts::run_scoped_fingerprint(text), + ); + } + _ => { + hash_bytes(&mut hash, source_kind_label(part.source_kind())); + hash_bytes(&mut hash, part.source()); + } + } hash } Before choosing this repair, decide whether the intended product contract is “replace the prior snapshot from this source” or “allow multiple snapshots.” A hash change without that decision would merely exchange one ambiguity for another. 8. Bounded verification Every Cargo command must use the wrapper. Run each once. A failing product assertion is a finding, not permission to edit production. IDExact commandTimeoutExpected terminal resultV00git diff --check main...HEAD -- $(cat "$lane/owned-paths.txt")30sExit 0, no outputV01./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test -p sk-protocol ai_reliability -- --nocapture300stest result: ok, zero failedV02./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh tree -p sk-protocol --edges normal,no-dev120sExit 0; receipt contains no script-kit-gpuiV03./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib ai::reliability -- --nocapture300sZero failedV04./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib ai::message_parts::tests -- --nocapture420sZero failedV05./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib ai::staged_context::tests -- --nocapture240sZero failedV06./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib ai::preflight_audit::tests -- --nocapture240sZero failedV07./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib ai::agent_chat::ui::thread::tests -- --nocapture600sZero failedV08./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib ai::agent_chat::ui::history_popup::tests -- --nocapture300sZero failedV09./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib ai::context_contract_integration_tests -- --nocapture300sZero failedV10./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib protocol::types::tests::get_elements -- --nocapture300sZero failedV11./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib protocol::types::tests::automation_window -- --nocapture240sZero failedV12./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib protocol::types::tests::wait_for -- --nocapture240sZero failedV13./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --test source_audit_ratchet -- --nocapture300sZero failed; no allowlist expansionV14./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh check --lib900sExit 0V15./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh build --bin script-kit-gpui900sExit 0; required only for runtime proof Capture each command: Zsh(set -o pipefail ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test -p sk-protocol ai_reliability -- --nocapture \ 2>&1 | tee "$lane/receipts/V01-domain-reliability.log" ) Use the same pattern for the remaining commands. Interpretation rules A compile failure caused by the branch is a confirmed regression. A test failure with a concrete production assertion is a confirmed regression. A source-audit failure is not automatically a product regression; inspect whether the behavior changed or the string lock is stale. A test green that never invokes the production symbol remains an unproven claim. A runtime fixture that never opens a real window or crosses the protocol boundary remains C3 at best. INVALID_INTERFERENCE receives one quiet rerun and is never counted green. Environmental or command-selection diagnosis gets one pass. At most one rerun is allowed. No production fix pass is authorized. A reproducible production failure is recorded and handed to the manager. 9. Screenshot request packet Screenshots are written only if the manager explicitly assigns this lane. Otherwise record the requests verbatim in 05-screenshot-requests.md. AI03-S01 — Typed recovery card State: Agent Chat after a classified usage-limit or Codex-upgrade failure. Required visible facts: - safe title - preservation copy - enabled recovery action - no raw JSON or provider internals - composer/transcript still intact Protocol sidecar: runtime/R01-recovery-get-elements.json Caption: “The card is a projection of the typed runtime failure—not a second guess based on formatted prose.” Does not prove: callback invocation, classification origin, or diagnostic isolation. AI03-S02 — Quiet Stop with preserved partial output State: User-stopped live turn after a distinctive partial UTF-8 answer. Required visible facts: - exact partial answer remains - no error row - composer is available - no misleading retry failure card Protocol sidecar: runtime/R02-stop-sequence.json Caption: “Stop preserves the work already received and exits as cancellation, not as a fabricated failure.” Does not prove: event ordering, queue pause, or cancellation kind; those require telemetry. AI03-S03 — Context lifecycle State: One pending context chip, one failed attachment, and one immutable used receipt. Required visible facts: - provenance cues differ - failed item is actionable/removable - immutable receipt is visibly non-removable - no private payload appears in labels Protocol sidecar: runtime/R03-context-elements.json Caption: “Context moves from proposed input to immutable receipt without exposing the attached payload to automation.” Does not prove: which bytes reached the provider. AI03-S04 — History popup with section boundaries State: Detached Agent Chat history popup with entries in all four date buckets; selection positioned after at least two headers. Required visible facts: - attached parent relationship - search field - section headers - selected row - action hints - selected row fully visible Protocol sidecar: runtime/R04-history-popup.json Caption: “A virtualized history list must navigate the visual list it renders, including its section headers.” Does not prove: focus restoration, stale-generation cleanup, or keyboard routing. AI03-S05 — Model mismatch/setup recovery State: Persisted requested model absent from runtime catalog. Required visible facts: - requested model is not silently replaced - mismatch is explained - candidates are available - performable recovery action is enabled Protocol sidecar: runtime/R05-model-mismatch.json Caption: “When the selected model disappears, the interface asks the user to recover instead of silently changing the engine.” Does not prove: that selecting a candidate reaches the runtime. Static screenshots must never be used as evidence for motion timing. No glass-motion screenshot or retuning belongs to this lane. 10. Article-ready integration hunks Write the selected final forms to 06-article-integration.md. Shared ledger hunk Markdown| Lane | Scope | Accounting | Improvements | Regressions | Proof gaps | Runtime proof | Evidence | |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---| | `03-ai-protocol` | AI reliability, Agent Chat, context, protocol projection, automation | `53/53` | `<count>` | `<confirmed>/<plausible>` | `<count>` | `<C4 result or Unverified>` | `.notes/oracle/branch-trust-audit/lanes/03-ai-protocol/08-worker-report.md` | Article section heading and core copy Use this section heading exactly: Markdown## AI reliability is only as strong as its last boundary Conditional green copy, usable only when the typed chain reaches C4: MarkdownThe branch does more than add a friendlier failure card. It introduces a typed reliability model, keeps user cancellation separate from provider failure, distinguishes required context from optional attachments, and gives automation an explicit, redacted projection of visible Agent Chat state. The important result is not any one type or test. It is that the same fact survives from the runtime boundary, through the reducer, into the renderer and `getElements` without being reclassified from prose or leaking diagnostic text. **Confidence:** Boundary verified **Evidence:** `.notes/oracle/branch-trust-audit/lanes/03-ai-protocol/04-verification.md` Fallback copy when runtime proof is unavailable: MarkdownThe branch introduces credible typed primitives for failure, cancellation, context preparation, and semantic element projection. Focused behavior tests support several of those contracts, but this audit did not accept them as runtime truth until the same state crossed a real Agent Chat window and the protocol boundary. The remaining gap is therefore explicit: strong internal models, incomplete end-to-end proof. **Confidence:** Behavior verified; runtime boundary unverified **Evidence:** `.notes/oracle/branch-trust-audit/lanes/03-ai-protocol/04-verification.md` Candidate finding hunk Include only findings whose local branch ownership and confidence are established: Markdown### Static fault lines worth fixing Two classes of defect are especially easy for AI-authored code to hide. First, a field can be named like an identity while carrying only a size: the preflight audit’s draft “fingerprint” currently collapses different equal-length drafts unless its consumers treat it as display-only metadata. Second, a popup can hold two coordinate systems at once: Agent Chat history selection is indexed over entries, while its virtualized visual list also contains date headers. Both issues have concrete falsifiers in the lane evidence and remain labeled according to the strongest proof actually obtained. **Confidence:** `<C2/C3/C4 per finding>` **Evidence:** `.notes/oracle/branch-trust-audit/lanes/03-ai-protocol/03-findings.jsonl` Screenshot caption hunk Markdown> **Screenshot — Typed recovery without diagnostic leakage.** The visible card > is derived from the runtime failure record, while the matching `getElements` > receipt exposes only safe text, semantic actions, and enabled state. > > Evidence: `.artifacts/branch-trust-audit/03-ai-protocol/<assigned-file>.png` 11. Largest article section — executable next-steps program This must be the largest substantive section contributed by the package. Use this exact heading: Markdown## The executable AI and protocol reliability program Use the following cards, updating only evidence IDs and final status. AI03-N01 — Preserve failure identity end to end Markdown**Priority:** P1 **Owner paths:** `crates/sk-protocol/src/ai_reliability/**`, `src/ai/reliability/**`, `src/ai/agent_chat/ui/thread.rs`, `src/ai/agent_chat/ui/components/setup_card.rs`, `src/ai/agent_chat/ui/components/transcript.rs` **Problem:** A typed provider/runtime fact is trustworthy only while its `AppFailureRecord` survives. Converting it to safe copy and classifying that copy again erases the original category and typically produces `Unknown`. **Change:** Remove any presentation-side reclassification. Pass the record or a typed presentation projection through every caller. Keep raw diagnostics inside the diagnostic vault. **Proof:** Provider-failure corpus, reducer test, live recovery card, `getElements`, semantic action invocation, export/storage canary scan. **Done when:** One correlation ID links the runtime fact, typed code, presentation, visible card, and element projection without raw diagnostic text. AI03-N02 — Make cancellation and retry boundary-proof Markdown**Priority:** P1 **Owner paths:** `ai_reliability/reducer.rs`, `agent_chat/ui/thread.rs`, `agent_chat/ui/view.rs` **Problem:** Stop, stream loss, retry, fork, and queue completion can converge on similar-looking UI while requiring different preservation and recovery semantics. **Change:** Keep cancellation, terminal loss with partial output, terminal loss without output, provider failure, and retry exhaustion as distinct typed paths. **Proof:** Exact-byte partial-output test plus a live Stop sequence; retry after composer/context mutation; queue-paused assertion; no duplicate user turn. **Done when:** Every terminal path has an explicit phase, preservation receipt, visible state, and protocol projection. AI03-N03 — Give preflight records real private identity Markdown**Priority:** P1 if consumed for freshness; otherwise P2 **Owner path:** `src/ai/preflight_audit.rs` **Problem:** Equal-length drafts currently share the same size-derived “fingerprint.” **Change:** Replace length-only identity with a run-scoped, length-framed salted digest. Decide and document whether the field means content identity, generation identity, or only size metadata. **Proof:** Equal-length collision test, no-cleartext serialization test, consumer audit, concurrent append/compaction test. **Done when:** A changed draft cannot inherit another draft’s preflight result, and the stored value is not a reusable dictionary oracle. AI03-N04 — Make context identity and lifetime explicit Markdown**Priority:** P1 **Owner paths:** `src/ai/message_parts.rs`, `src/ai/staged_context.rs`, `agent_chat/ui/thread.rs` **Problem:** Context has several identities: source, snapshot, visible chip, prepared payload, and immutable receipt. Collapsing them can silently replace or duplicate user-selected material. **Change:** Document identity per context variant. Preserve explicit primary/supplemental roles, generation, provenance, and lifetime. Decide whether same-source text is replacement or accumulation. **Proof:** Same-source/different-content test, accepted/unaccepted send tests, retry/fork tests, live element projection, private-payload scan. **Done when:** Every context item has one documented transition from pending to failed or immutable receipt, with no silent loss. AI03-N05 — Repair history popup indexing and lifecycle Markdown**Priority:** P1 for offscreen selection; P2 for lifecycle-only defects **Owner paths:** `history_popup.rs`, `popup_automation.rs`, `view/portal_host.rs`, `chat_window.rs` **Problem:** Logical entry order, visual list order, section-header insertion, window generation, parent focus, and portal replacement are independent state axes. **Change:** Map entry identity to visual list index, centralize close/reopen generation handling, cancel rejected portals, and use shared popup/list/token owners. **Proof:** Four-bucket navigation test, rapid reopen runtime probe, parent-close probe, automation registry receipt, keyboard/mouse parity. **Done when:** The selected row is visible, stale windows cannot remove current ones, and every close route restores or deliberately declines focus. AI03-N06 — Make getElements the authoritative AI projection Markdown**Priority:** P1 **Owner paths:** protocol query constructors/variants, `agent_chat_state.rs`, `elements_actions_scriptlets.rs`, Agent Chat view collector **Problem:** A rendered recovery control or context chip that automation cannot observe is not proven and cannot be operated reliably. **Change:** Derive renderer and collector from the same typed presentation facts. Project explicit quality, reason codes, role-safe actions, focus, selection, and redacted content. **Proof:** Live `getElements` in ready, streaming, cancelled, failed, setup, permission, context-failure, model-mismatch, and popup states. **Done when:** Every visible shared AI control has one stable semantic element, and no hidden/raw content is returned. AI03-N07 — Replace source assertions with behavior receipts Markdown**Priority:** P2 **Owner paths:** `agent_chat/ui/tests.rs`, `thread/tests.rs`, protocol tests **Problem:** A substring or occurrence-count test can stay green while the feature is unreachable, its callback is absent, or its I/O is broken. **Change:** Move invariants upward: compiler exhaustiveness, direct reducer tests, GPUI behavior tests, and runtime window/protocol probes. Parameterize filesystem roots where real I/O needs isolation. **Proof:** Source-audit inventory does not grow; overclaiming tests are replaced by production-symbol calls; the ordinary source-audit ratchet remains green. **Done when:** Test names describe what the test actually executes. AI03-N08 — Establish a finite release gate Markdown**Priority:** P2 **Owner:** manager/lane 6 integration **Problem:** Reliability improvements can regress independently across the domain model, app adapter, renderer, storage, popup lifecycle, and protocol. **Change:** Add one finite release matrix that reuses existing focused tests and runtime probes. Do not create a parallel framework. **Gate:** 1. domain reducer tests; 2. app classification/presentation tests; 3. context preparation and staged-lifetime tests; 4. Agent Chat thread/history tests; 5. protocol serialization tests; 6. source-audit ratchet; 7. live failure, Stop, popup, Quick AI, and `getElements` receipts. **Done when:** A single bounded run reports each layer independently, preserves its terminal logs, and refuses to convert skipped runtime proof into green. 12. Completion and stop conditions The lane is complete only when all of the following are true: 01-path-accounting.tsv contains 53 unique data rows. No row remains UNREVIEWED. Every changed path has a diff artifact, review state, and evidence reference. Every material claim is C2–C4 or explicitly labeled C0/C1. Runtime claims are C4 or explicitly Unverified. Focused checks have terminal receipts and exit codes. No failing product assertion was “fixed” by weakening a test. No source-audit allowlist was expanded. Screenshot requests identify exact state, crop, caption, sidecar, and proof limitation. 06-article-integration.md contains the ledger row, article section, screenshot caption, and next-step cards. Remaining risks are severity-ranked. The non-lane worktree state matches the captured pre-existing state. No production file was edited. No commit, push, merge, app deployment, or article publication occurred. Final non-lane mutation check: Zshgit status --porcelain=v1 --untracked-files=all | grep -v '^?? \.notes/oracle/branch-trust-audit/lanes/03-ai-protocol/' \ > "$lane/receipts/99-final-nonlane-worktree.txt" || true diff -u \ "$lane/receipts/00-preexisting-worktree.txt" \ "$lane/receipts/99-final-nonlane-worktree.txt" \ > "$lane/receipts/99-nonlane-worktree-delta.diff" || true If the delta contains changes attributable to this worker, stop and report the boundary violation. Never reset, discard, or rewrite another worker’s changes. Explicitly excluded production remediation; speculative Agent Chat redesign; new UI or protocol frameworks; duplicate runtime harnesses; glass-motion retuning; test weakening; broad adjacent protocol migration; commits, pushes, merges, deployment, or publication.

