03-ai-protocol — patch-ready audit execution packet The attached ownership list contains exactly 53 paths, and the supplied delta is 5,421 insertions and 2,162 deletions. The PackX bundle contains only 13 selected files, so it is useful for seeding hypotheses but cannot close coverage; every finding must be checked against the local main...HEAD diff. attachment-0002-a4d79578bf5dbe3… attachment-0003-8e4d9a480f61046… attachment-0001-0780b6cb8cffb4c… The audit must enforce four repository rules throughout: Carry the typed AppFailureRecord from runtime fact to presentation; never reclassify formatted safe copy. Keep raw provider diagnostics out of UI and automation output. Treat user Stop as cancellation, not failure. Do not claim a rendered recovery/context control is proven unless the live getElements projection exposes it from the same state source. attachment-0001-0780b6cb8cffb4c… Source-reading tests are proof debt unless no higher rung can express the invariant. Behavior tests, GPUI tests, and runtime probes outrank include_str!, substring assertions, and occurrence-count assertions. attachment-0001-0780b6cb8cffb4c… 1. First implementation action Run this from the repository root. It records the pre-existing multiplayer tree, installs the exact ownership list inside the lane, measures the current target, checks that every owned path still belongs to main...HEAD, and writes the first audit artifact. Zshset -euo pipefail repo="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" cd "$repo" branch="$(git branch --show-current)" base_sha="$(git rev-parse main)" head_sha="$(git rev-parse HEAD)" merge_base_sha="$(git merge-base main HEAD)" commit_count="$(git rev-list --count main..HEAD)" global_path_count="$(git diff --name-only main...HEAD | LC_ALL=C sort -u | wc -l | tr -d ' ')" global_shortstat="$(git diff --shortstat main...HEAD)" preexisting_status="$(git status --porcelain=v1 --untracked-files=all)" lane=".notes/oracle/branch-trust-audit/lanes/03-ai-protocol" mkdir -p "$lane"/{diff